---
description: Rules for the default OpenRouter chat backend and the LiteLLM backend inside LLM chat elements.
globs: "**/llm_chat/**/*.py"
---
- `LLMChatElement` defaults `backend` to `openrouter`, which uses `OpenRouterChatModel`. `generate_response` converts payloads with `_messages_to_openrouter` and calls `client.chat.send_async`. `create_model_selector_view` defaults `provider` to OpenAI, and the OpenRouter selector lists OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, xAI, Mistral, and Meta.
- `backend='litellm'` uses `LiteLLMChatModel`. Its `generate_response` converts payloads with `_messages_to_litellm` and calls `litellm.acompletion`. Its selector lists OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, xAI, Groq, Mistral, and OpenRouter, plus Custom when models are passed.
- `langchain-text-splitters` splits text in the chunker. It does not perform chat completions.
